From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:15:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] game/fft: four observation gates on the pillarbox candidates
 (0077 pre-work: name the site that still confines the picture)

The wide pair, both pools, the wide-viewport cut and the screen-shape chain are all active and the host presents 1920x888, yet the device's picture is still the game's own drawing confined to a centered 16:9 (a 1578.67x888 content rect). The gates record what the letterbox fitter's one non-null-rect call (main+0x46f2b0) and its compare/select block (main+0x45f988), the post-cut wide-viewport branch (main+0x8ed18) and the camera aspect store (main+0xdc5dc, camera+0xcd8, plus the first-layer chain the PC port's fix hides the pillarbox sprite through) see at run time, one tab-separated line per hit in Documents/pillarbox_probe.txt (PB_CALL / PB_RECT / VP_CLAMP / CAM tags, 60 MB cap), read-only.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: FFT 1.5.1's picture is still confined to a centered 16:9 in the game's own drawing past the wide-viewport cuts: the host presents 1920x888 but the content rect is 1578.67x888. Four read-only observation gates record what the letterbox fitter's call and output, the post-cut wide-viewport branch and the camera aspect store see, until a run names the site that confines it; the host side is dm/host/hle_pillarbox.c (Documents/pillarbox_probe.txt, 60 MB cap)
Issue: mexicanstratocaster/NX2Apple-edgy#1

