 Open follow-ups, in order: the movies (the game letterboxes its own 16:9 movies; check they center on the wide picture), the touch layout at the taller picture (it followed the pair at 720 height on 1.4.0), and the messy textures in cutscenes and battle (see Open below).
 
+**Still pillarboxed with all of that (2026-11-21, open).** With the wide pair, both pools, the wide-viewport cut and the screen-shape chain all active (0074-0076), the device session's log shows every host stage wide (`DM_SCREEN_ASPECT=2.173` → `screen shape 2.173 wide: output 1920x880` → swap chain 1920x888 → `WindowCrop 0,0 1920x888` → `present: picture shape 1920x888`, `the game's view follows it`) - and the battlefield is *still* a centered 16:9: the phone's USB screenshots measure the in-texture content at a 1578.67x888 rect (bars 170.67 tex px, the geometry the picture-fill would put there), so the confinement happens in the game's own drawing, past the cut. Static search cleared the known candidates: `0x45f7d0`'s 16:9 clamp is dead code (its only caller passes a real rect), and the binary holds no other stored 16:9 constant. Four observation gates (the profile's `OBS`, this run's `PB_CALL` / `PB_RECT` / `VP_CLAMP` / `CAM` lines in `Documents/pillarbox_probe.txt`, hle_pillarbox.c) now record what the letterbox fitter's call and output, the post-cut wide-viewport branch and the camera aspect store see, to name the site that confines it; the PC port's widescreen fix (NexusMods FFTacticsFix) replaced five coordinated places there (the letterbox viewport calculator, the first-layer pillarbox sprite, a camera-center offset, two parallax offsets behind WorldToScreen, and the grain filter gate), a shape to mirror, not offsets to copy.
+
 ## Open
 
 - **Messy textures in cutscenes and battle** (newspaper-print noise over the picture on an iPhone 18 Pro Max, 1080p 16:9 build). The prime leads, in order: upstream [issue #2275](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/2275)'s `sampler ID 768 not registered` (one line per session in this game's device logs too, once read as benign - it drives every third frame of the CRI Mana movies and in-engine sprites to horizontal streaks, and a host fix for reading such samplers, SeparateSamplerId raw IDs from uniform-buffer words, landed 2026-11-12 and is in this engine); the 19 unbounded shader keys of `c1_full` from the update's shader build (bindings whose slot was not decoded); the 30 texture/cover pixel pairs of the DmIOS shader audit. All three sit in the project's handoff evidence; a device log of a messy-textures session with `DM_NVN_TEXINFO=1280x720` is the next probe.
